jobs.description:
Under direct supervision of the Head of Programmes, the Programme Coordinator (Humanitarian Response and Recovery (HRR)) will be responsible and accountable for coordination of IOM’s operations in response to the HRR challenges in IOM Chad.

**Responsibilities**

1. Coordinate and monitor the implementation of all operational and administrative aspects of emergency-related projects, ensuring effectiveness, coherence, integrity, and the application of the organization’s policies and procedures.
2. Work in close collaboration with the Chief of Mission (CoM) to ensure that all the components of the emergency response and the regular recovery and development activities operate in a coherent and mutually supportive manner.
3. Ensure adequate IOM’s Response Preparedness by:
• Improving coordination in the response preparedness capacity of programmes.
• Verifying and facilitating alignment of programmatic response preparedness with inter-sector common planning frameworks.
• Coordinating the implementation of the preparedness efforts envisaged by IOM at different sectors.
4. Keep abreast of humanitarian policies, international standards and best practices relating to the emergency field; recommend how cross-cutting issues including gender, age, education, disability, environment and protection can be better incorporated for further enhancement of the cross-border humanitarian response.
5. Ensure timely preparation and submission of all emergency project reports according to IOM and donor formats as required. Coordinate preparation of regular updates, project summaries, lessons learnt, press releases and other relevant materials.
6. Guide and supervise staff responsible for the implementation of emergency projects. Coordinate training for staff on emergency response to promote a common understanding and knowledge of ways and means to strengthen the humanitarian response.
7. Identify new opportunities for emergency response and participate in the development of emergency project proposals in coordination with the Resources Management Unit, Department of Humanitarian Response & Recovery (DHRR), the Regional Office, and Program/Project Managers.
8. Ensure the provision of timely, accurate, standardized, and adequate information to all relevant stakeholders regarding movements, new displacements, mobility trends, and conditions in return/relocation areas, paying special attention to the situation of vulnerable groups. Liaise with donor representatives and periodically brief them on current and planned programs in order to mobilize necessary financial support.
9. Participate actively in various fora, including inter-agency coordination groups, and meetings with governmental authorities, non-governmental organizations, donors, and other stakeholders.
10. Undertake duty travel relating to need assessments, emergency project monitoring, liaison with counterparts, problem-solving, and new project development, as required.
11. Perform such other duties as may be assigned.

**Required Qualifications and Experience**

**Education**

- Master’s degree in International Relations, Political Science, Business, or Public Administration or a related field from an accredited academic institution with five years of relevant professional experience; or,
- University degree in the above fields with seven years of relevant professional experience.

Accredited Universities are those listed in the UNESCO World Higher Education Database.

**Experience**

- Demonstrated managerial experience in fields related to IOM emergency programming, including emergency coordination, Non-Food Items (NFI)/ shelter, Camp Coordination and Camp Management (CCCM), Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM), protection, transition & recovery, or preparedness and response, in conflict/post conflict, Hardship Duty Stations is mandatory;
- Demonstrated experience in managing a large number of teams across several diverse emergency response and humanitarian assistance thematic areas;
- Proven managerial and administrative experience in emergency programmes in conflict, post-conflict, and complex emergencies in hardship locations in varied regions is required;
- Experience in managing programmes within or supporting the Office of the Under-Secretary -General (USG) of the Office for the Coordination of Humanitarian Affairs (OCHA) is highly advantageous;
- Demonstrated experience in coordination and humanitarian experience is mandatory;
- Practical experience in IOM project management, including administrative and financial management, procurement and Human Resources (HR) procedures, and internal control procedures;
- Experience working in an emergency context and ability to liaise with government officials, donors, UN personnel, Non-Governmental Organizations (NGO), and other stakeholders;
- Demonstrated experience in non-family hardship duty stations is mandatory; and,
- Demonstrated experience in implementing Humanitarian Principles in complex conflict/post conflict emergencies in IOM is highly advantageous.

**Skills**

- Demonstrated judgment, ability to extract, interpret, analyse and format data and make decisions rapidly to resolve operational problems;
- Ability to work with minimum supervision;
- Emergency Response and Induction Training (ERIT) and Senior Emergency Leadership and Coordination (SELAC) trainings are advantageous;
- IOM Programme Management and Humanitarian Expertise in complex post-conflict hardship locations are desired;
- Capacity to work effectively in high-pressure, rapidly changing environments;
- Excellent communication, negotiation and coordination skills;
- Demonstrated knowledge of IOM Project Management Handbook, WAVE, Project Information and Management Application (PRIMA);
- Demonstrated computer skills, including proficiency in the MS Office package (Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook); and,
- Familiarity with WAVE is highly recommended.

**Languages**

For this position, fluency in English and French is required (oral and written).

Working knowledge of another official UN languages (Arabic, Chinese, Russian, and Spanish) is an advantage.

Proficiency of language(s) required will be specifically evaluated during the selection process, which may include written and/or oral assessments.

Under the overall supervision of the Chief of Mission (COM) and the direct supervision of the Head of Programmes, in close coordination with the Regional Thematic Specialist (RTS) and the Immigration and Border Governance (IBG) Division, the Programme Coordinator (IBG) will be responsible for managing, coordinating, and overseeing the activities of the relevant IBG Programme.

**Responsibilities**

1. Coordinate the overall implementation of the IBG portfolio, including, but not limited to, projects focusing on border management information systems, regular pathways, regularization, readmission cooperation, admission and stay channels, immigration policy, legal identity, counter-migrant smuggling, border and development/trade initiatives, and Humanitarian Border Management, to ensure their impact, effectiveness, coherence and integrity, and their timely completion, in line with IOM’s policies, practices and the donor’s contractual requirements.
2. Provide technical inputs for the development of policy and operational resources aimed at enhancing safe, orderly, and regular migration pathways through the implementation of immigration and border governance policies and tools.
3. Provide guidance and substantive support to the Regional Office and Country Offices (COs), in coordination with IBG RTS, on emerging national and regional trends, donor priorities, and resource mobilization for the development and execution of IBG projects.
4. Provide operational guidance and technical supervision on IBG projects, including managing and providing technical support to relevant programme staff, and capacity development initiatives.
5. Coordinate and conduct capacity-development activities in coordination with technical experts on IBG thematic areas including, but not limited to, document security, passport examination, legal identity, identity management, the responsible use of biometrics, readmission, cooperation, admission and stay pathways, and Advance Passenger Information, amongst others.
6. Establish and maintain close and effective working relationships with government counterparts at the technical level, to guide project implementation and the resolution of implementation-related challenges, including organizing periodical meetings with relevant stakeholders.
7. Oversee the elaboration of public information and training materials, including resources for customs, border and immigration authorities, visa officers, and other border governance stakeholders for internal and external use, in coordination with IBG Specialists and other relevant Divisions.
8. Pursue the establishment of partnerships with UN Agencies, humanitarian organizations, government, and community interlocutors, and with a broad range of stakeholders towards the successful implementation of IBG programmes.
9. Contribute to advance IBG thematic areas within the respective UN Network on Migration (UNNM) and other initiatives related to institutional efforts to implement the Global Compact for Migration (GCM) and strengthen migration governance.
10. Undertake travel duty as required to strengthen, coordinate and/or support programme implementation.
11. Perform such duties as may be assigned.

**Required Qualifications and Experience**

**Education**

- Master’s degree in International Relations, Political Science, Humanitarian Affairs, Economic Development, Business or Public Administration, International Studies or a related field from an accredited academic institution with five years of relevant professional experience; or,
- University degree in the above fields with seven years of relevant professional experience.

Accredited Universities are those listed in the UNESCO World Higher Education Database.

**Experience**

- Experience in programme conceptualisation, development, monitoring, reporting and evaluation;
- Experience in programme development and capacity-development activities;
- Experience in liaising with governmental and diplomatic authorities as well as with national and international institutions;
- Demonstrated experience in financial and business administration;
- Demonstrated experience and proven understanding of internal and international migration issues in the country and in the region;
- Experience in organizing consultations, workshops and seminars with high-level stakeholders;
- Demonstrated experience and in-depth knowledge of the broad range of migration-related subject areas dealt with by the Organization; and,
- Demonstrated experience and knowledge of UN and bilateral donor programming.

**Skills**

- Proven ability to establish and maintain strong working relations with relevant Government counterparts, international organizations and private sector entities;
- Excellent leadership, coordination, and information management skills;
- Detailed knowledge of the UN System, Non-Governmental Organizations and other international organizations/institutions;
- Demonstrated knowledge of migration data, labour migration patterns in the relevant region and ability to negotiate with government authorities;
- Demonstrated knowledge of human and financial resources management;
- Demonstrated conceptualization, analytical, and writing skills;
- Demonstrated communication, organizational, and interpersonal relationship skills;
- Proven ability to meet deadlines and work under pressure with minimum supervision; and,
- Proven ability to establish and maintain partnerships with development partners, government counterparts, UN agencies, local authorities and other relevant stakeholders.

**Languages**

For this position, fluency in English and French is required (oral and written).

Working knowledge of another official UN languages (Arabic, Chinese, Russian, and Spanish) is an advantage.

Proficiency of language(s) required will be specifically evaluated during the selection process, which may include written and/or oral assessments.

***This position is open to candidates with existing work authorization in the location where the position is advertised.***

**IRC Background:** The mission of the International Rescue Committee (IRC) is to help people whose lives and livelihoods are shattered by conflict and disaster to survive, recover and gain control of their future. Founded in 1933, the IRC has a presence in over 40 countries and 27 offices in the United States; the IRC leads the way from harm to home. Domestically, our offices across the U.S. ensure new arrivals have food, shelter, and clothing, and work with refugees to help them gain self-sufficiency.

**Job Overview:**

The IRC in Sacramento’s Financial Capabilities department supports English Language Learners and low- to moderate-income individuals in building their knowledge and skills in navigating US financial systems. As part of this aim, the IRC has facilitated the Volunteer Income Tax Assistance Project, providing free tax preparation services for these community members.

Under the supervision of the Financial Empowerment Center Program Manager, the Tax Site Coordinator supports the coordination and day-to-day administration of the IRC’s National Volunteer Income Tax Assistance (VITA) program in Sacramento, California. IRC’s goal is to assist 4,000 taxpayers nationally, and 150 locally, in preparing their returns in a safe, culturally and linguistically appropriate manner.

**Major Responsibilities:**

- Oversee the day-to-day operations of the IRC’s Volunteer Income Tax Assistance (VITA) site during tax season (January – April 2025), including but not limited to:
- Creation of scheduling system for client appointments at each site
- Coordinating and providing technical support to volunteer tax preparers
- Supervision of virtual and in-person volunteer tax preparers
- Providing customer service to taxpayers, as needed
- Conducting quality reviews and electronically filing tax returns;
- Schedule customers for tax preparation
- Facilitate the launch of the VITA program including but not limited to:
- Recruitment and vetting of tax preparer volunteers
- Solidifying each site’s plan for tax intake and document collection
- Train volunteers on tax preparation process
- Conduct outreach for VITA program
- Complete the IRS Link and Learn tax training at the Advanced level as well as the Site Coordinator Training;
- Assist with data collection and reporting;
- Ensure compliance with IRS and VITA program policies and procedures, as well as IRC policies;
- Other duties as assigned

**Job Requirements:**

- Undergraduate degree in finance, accounting, or a related field; or mix of equivalent years of related work experience and education preferred;
- Previous experience as a VITA volunteer strongly preferred;
- Previous experience with personal income tax preparation strongly preferred;
- Experience in a non-profit organization preferred;
- Excellent customer service skills, including experience working with a diverse client base;
- Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to make presentations as well as the ability to supervise a large, diverse group of volunteers;
- Strong organizational skills and high level of attention to detail;
- High level of computer literacy; familiarity with TaxSlayer software highly preferred;
- High level of comfort, functioning and effectiveness in multi-cultural and multi-disciplinary teams;
- Strong commitment to economic empowerment of low-income and underserved populations;
- Excellent written and verbal English;

**Position Reports to: Financial Empowerment Center Program Manager**

**Position directly supervises: Interns and volunteers**

**Indirect Reporting: Site Director**

**Other Internal and/or external contacts:**

**Internal: IRC program staff, interns and volunteers**

**External: Community partners and economic empowerment programs.**

**Working Environment*****:***

This role has a hybrid work environment with a mix of virtual and in-office days. The current hybrid schedule may change. The schedule includes:

- **Virtual Work:** Some days will be fully remote, allowing you to work from home.
- **In-Office Work:** Certain days will require you to be present in our main office; Standard, professional office environment;
- Some evening and weekend work hours will be required;
- Home internet required

**Compensation:** (Pay Rate: $32.15/hr). Ranges are based on various factors including the labor market, job type, internal equity, and budget. Exact offers are calibrated by work location, individual candidate experience and skills relative to the defined job requirements.

**Equal Opportunity Employer:** IRC is an Equal Opportunity Employer. IRC considers all applicants on the basis of merit without regard to race, sex, color, national origin, religion, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, disability or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.

**Professional Standards:** All International Rescue Committee workers must adhere to the core values and principles outlined in IRC Way - Standards for Professional Conduct. Our Standards are Integrity, Service, Equality and Accountability. In accordance with these values, the IRC operates and enforces policies on Safeguarding, Conflicts of Interest, Fiscal Integrity, and Reporting Wrongdoing and Protection from Retaliation. IRC is committed to take all necessary preventive measures and create an environment where people feel safe, and to take all necessary actions and corrective measures when harm occurs. IRC builds teams of professionals who promote critical reflection, power sharing, debate, and objectivity to deliver the best possible services to our clients.

**US Benefits:** We offer a comprehensive and highly competitive set of benefits. In the US, these include: 10 sick days, 10 US holidays, 20-25 paid time off days depending on role and tenure, medical insurance starting at $163 per month, dental starting at $6.50 per month, and vision starting at $5 per month, FSA for healthcare and commuter costs, a 403b retirement savings plans with immediately vested matching, disability & life insurance, and an Employee Assistance Program which is available to our staff and their families to support counseling and care in times of crisis and mental health struggles.

JOB PURPOSE: Lead and manage the Oxfam Syria team working in the eastern hub, overseeing programs and support. This includes representation, partnerships management, and coordination with all external stakeholders, designing the right projects, ensuring quality implementation and outcomes of ongoing projects, and identifying and seeking opportunities for early recovery and humanitarian interventions. The Area Manager leads the whole team with a fully functional base to
deliver a program in an effective and efficient way.

KEY RESPONSIBILITIES
General
•Oversee the quality implementation of Oxfam’s program in respective hub (usually multiple governorates from one field office);
•Represent Oxfam at the governorate level. Establish and maintain working and collaborative relationships with relevant stakeholders in these two governorates, this includes governorate and district authorities, local organizations and communities, contractors, and international organizations. Secure their continuous support for Oxfam’s work in the governorate, by ensuring effective communication about Oxfam and its work, including Oxfam’s overall purpose and goals as well as specific program objectives in the area;
•Participate in relevant external coordination meetings including those called for by governorate authorities, UN/OCHA, or other relevant stakeholders;
•Take overall responsibility for the implementation of Oxfam’s Country Strategy (OCS) in the respective hub. This includes a) the implementation of project grants; b) the identification of opportunities for further humanitarian interventions; c) regular consultations with Oxfam country office managers for initiatives that contribute to the implementation of the OCS;
•Supervise the work of Team Leaders and other senior staff at the hub
•Continuously evaluate developments on the ground as related to humanitarian and recovery needs and advise the country office on needed humanitarian interventions;
•Ensure regular communication with Oxfam country office in Damascus in order to ensure head office is informed in a timely manner of significant new developments on the ground that affect/may affect program implementation

Project design, implementation and partnerships management
•Overall responsibility for quality implementation of project grants at hub level
•Ensure all Team Leaders are fully familiar and understand the objectives, log frame and budgets of the project proposals they are responsible for implementing;
•Support field department heads at hub level in developing project work plans and budgets based on planned project outputs and results. Oversee their implementation;
•Support Team Leaders and other senior staff in proactively identifying and managing potential obstacles and risks to project implementation and in taking initiatives to mitigate these;
•Support Team Leaders in coordinating with Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability and Learning (MEAL) team to track performance monitoring analysis and adjust implementation accordingly; in cooperation with the MEAL department identify and synthesis best practices and lessons learned. Ensure these are shared with head office and that senior field staff incorporates these in further implementation;
•Support the Team Leaders in monitoring, procurement, delivery and/or installation of project materials and services;
•Ensure all projects are implemented according to both Oxfam’s and donors’ requirements;
•Ensure project staff implements activities according to global humanitarian minimum standards and best practice, among which Core Humanitarian Standards, Sphere standards, Charter for Change;
•Perform biweekly visits to projects site in order to track implementation.
•Manage partnerships and ensure proper coordination to deliver the program.
•Lead regular needs assessment in the hub area to define priorities and design program
•Lead proposal design with support of the funding team, advisers and Program Coordinator
•Lead partnership management at the hub level
•Provide direction and exploration on early recovery and resilience program at hub level

Finance, procurement, logistics, and administration:
•Ensure that Oxfam’s financial and procurement policies are strictly adhered to. Work in collaboration with Oxfam Damascus country office to ensure proper and timely finance and procurement processes;
•Support department heads at the hub level in developing and updating monthly budget spending plans based on planned activities and in cooperation with the finance department;
•Support Team Leaders in taking immediate remedial steps in case of over or under-spending;
•Ensure all logistics are in place to facilitate project implementation;
•Supervise requests for procurement orders.
•Safeguard the budget and manage financial risks
•Ensure right work environment and safe workplace

Human Resource:
•Ensure that Oxfam Syria Human Resources policies are correctly implemented;
•Ensure a proper overview of staffing needs overall project grants;
•In coordination with Oxfam HR department at the country office in Damascus, hire support staff required for the field office;
•Ensure all program staff have a good understanding of the project’s objectives, the logical framework and budget of the project they are hired under;
•In cooperation with the Human Resource department at country office and department heads, ensure hired staff are properly trained in Oxfam basic standards (safeguarding, gender, protection, code of conduct), in humanitarian standards, and as may otherwise be required to perform their tasks;
•Support the field team to achieve objectives through ongoing support and regular meetings, including discussions on progress against objectives/implementation plan, providing feedback and encouragement;
•Identify and propose professional and personal development of staff;
•Perform performance appraisal of staff directly supervised according to Oxfam standards.

Reporting, documentation, relationships management and donor engagement
•In coordination Team leaders, advisers, funding team and Program Coordinator ensure timely and quality preparation and submission of Oxfam and donor narrative and financial reports. This includes Oxfam internal monthly reports, weekly sit-reps and reports of external meetings;
•Report any incident that must be brought to Oxfam's attention (e.g. security, accountability, safeguarding, code of conduct, external interference);
•Collaborate with the MEAL and comms team to document project implementation through photographs, videos or blogs; - facilitate access of communications staff to field locations; and provide other materials and information that supports Oxfam’s strategic communications.
•Strictly adhere to Oxfam’s data protection standards for beneficiaries, partners and staff in regard to data collected for project purposes.
•With the support of senior management team and funding team; support on donor engagement and hosting donor visits.
•Leads the relationships management and coordination at his/her office and represents Oxfam.

Security management and new emergencies
•Fully adhere to Oxfam security protocols and procedures and ensure that all staff do so;
•Contribute to ongoing security management and planning as necessary;
•Report any incident that must be brought to Oxfam's attention (e.g. security, accountability, safeguarding, code of conduct, external interference).
•Regularly assess hub areas and inform the Program Coordinator to prioritize humanitarian programming.
•Roll out a preparedness plan and ensure capacity to respond ‘emergency in an emergency’. Where necessary, ready to be deployed for new emergencies in other areas of the country

**About World Vision**

World Vision is one of the world's leading humanitarian development and advocacy organizations, operating in nearly 100 countries worldwide, including Georgia. For more information, please visit www.wvi.org/georgia.

**Invitation to Apply**

World Vision Georgia Abkhazia Program invites qualified Individual Consultants to apply for the facilitation of structured Reflective Wellbeing, Resilience and Peer Support sessions during the final capacity building workshop for four partner civil society organisations (CSOs) under the European Union-funded “Building Resilient Communities in Abkhazia” project, implemented in consortium with Action Against Hunger and Danish Refugee Council.

**Scope of Work**

After two years of demanding implementation, workshop participants need space to pause, release stress and reconnect as peers. The consultant will design and lead sessions that may include team-building games, informal peer support circles, stress management practices and mediation sessions, applying gender-sensitive and gender-responsive approaches throughout. Key deliverables:

- Sessions facilitation plan and session materials, submitted prior to the workshop;
- Facilitation of two 2-hour sessions within the workshop agenda (remotely, in Russian);
- Consultancy Report using the provided template, covering achievements, challenges and recommendations for continued CSO capacity development.

**Required Qualifications and Experience**

- Proven experience in facilitating capacity building events for CSOs or similar civil society actors;
- Experience designing and delivering participatory training and reflective learning methodologies;
- Relevant university degree (social sciences, development studies, education or similar);
- Good oral communication skills in Russian; English is a significant asset;
- Ability to work independently with minimal supervision;
- Cross-cultural sensitivity, flexibility and emotional maturity;
- Proficiency in producing professional, well-structured documents;
- Demonstrated awareness and application of Child Protection and Gender mainstreaming principles.

**Timeframe**

The consultancy will take place in November 2026, for a total of two (2) working days:

- Development of workshop materials and session plans - 0.5 day - Home-based
- Delivery of two remote workshop sessions (November 7–8, 2026; 2 hrs each) - 1 day - Home-based (Zoom or similar)
- Development of Consultancy Report with recommendations - 0.5 day - Home-based

**Budget**

The consultancy operates on a lump-sum basis. All costs, including professional fees and applicable taxes, must be covered within the lump sum, and a detailed budget breakdown must be included in the offer. Payment will be made upon satisfactory completion of all deliverables and acceptance of the Consultancy Report.

**Evaluation Criteria**

Applications will be evaluated at World Vision's discretion. Criteria include, but are not limited to: quality, reputation and performance in providing the services; relevant previous experience; thoroughness of the information provided; competitive pricing with demonstrated capacity to deliver; and ability to deliver within the agreed timeframe. Technical and financial proposals will be evaluated separately, and the contract will be awarded to the least-cost technically acceptable proposal.

Créée en 1922, DanChurchAid (DCA) est une organisation non gouvernementale Danoise dont l’action est basée sur les droits. Installée en RCA depuis 2015, DCA fournit une assistance aux communautés les plus démunies en situation de conflit et de post-conflit au travers de son Programme d’Action Humanitaire «Communautés Plus Sûres » : éducation aux risques des Armes Légères et Petit Calibres (ALPC), des Restes et Explosifs de Guerre (REG) ; Réduction de la Violence Armée (RVA) et consolidation de la paix & Support Psycho social , distribution des biens non alimentaires et ménagers (NFI), Cash conditionnel et inconditionnel (coupons alimentaires, etc), distribution des semences et outils, appui aux organisations de la Société Civile pour leur implication dans la réforme du Secteur de Sécurité (RSS).

DCA recherche **Un Chef d’Equipe (Team Leader)** trèsexpérimentés pour participer au développement et la mise en œuvre des activités Bria.

**OBJECTIF DU POSTE :**

Sous la supervision du Chef de projet FH, le Team Leader est chargé de la coordination et gestion des activités dans le cadre du Projet FH dans les localités de Bria. Il/elle est aussi responsable de la gestion de l’équipe. Le/la Team Leader est responsable de la représentation de DCA auprès du groupe de travail sécurité alimentaire et distribution cash et des structures techniques étatiques de Bria. Il/elle rend compte directement au Chef de projet sur tous les aspects programmatiques et opérationnels, et maintient une forte collaboration technique.

**RÔLES ET RESPONSABILITÉS :**

1. **Gestion et Coordination de programme**

- Mettre en place un plan d’implémentation détaillé des activités, un plan de dépenses et d’achat, et les actualiser régulièrement et veiller à leur mise en œuvre ;
- Effectuer la planification, la coordination et la supervision des activités en étroite collaboration avec le / la Chef de Projet ;
- S’assurer que les responsabilités et les tâches de tous les membres de l’équipe sont exécutées convenablement et en conformité avec les planifications hebdomadaires et mensuelles ;
- Sous la supervision technique du Chef de Projet, développer les outils, les SOP et les directives techniques des activités, et faciliter les formations de l’équipe ;
- Produire des rapports mensuels et contractuels assortis des résultats atteints, des bonnes pratiques et leçons apprises, ainsi que de la situation observée ;
- Fournir un appui technique et opérationnel adéquats à l’équipe sur le terrain, y compris dans la production de rapports sur l’état d’avancement des activités et les progrès accomplis en détaillant les défis et les recommandations pour action ;
- Effectuer des missions fréquentes sur le terrain et visites du projet ;
- Superviser la réalisation des évaluations rapides conduites, en coordination avec le Chef de Projet et rédiger les rapports d’évaluation ;
- Veiller à ce que les données soient collectées, stockées, archivées, traitées, analysées et diffusées selon des modalités éthiques, conformément aux protocoles internes de protection des données ;
- Faciliter le développement et la distribution de matériel d’information, d’éducation et de communication (IEC) qui intègrent des messages de sensibilisation contextualisés et pertinents sur les questions liées à la prévention des violences basées sur le genre (VBG), les droits et la protection de l'enfant (PE);
- Superviser les sensibilisations Communautaires;
- Participer activement aux réunions de coordination avec les partenaires, le cluster et les différents groupes de travail (y compris le GTPE et VBG), les autorités (Affaire humanitaire et Affaire sociale);
- Participer au suivi et évaluation du projet ;
- Assurer la connaissance et la diffusion des mécanismes de redevabilité du Projet ;
- Adhérer complètement aux engagements et règlements établis dans la Politique de Protection des Participants aux Programmes et le Code de Conduite de DCA, y compris le respectde confidentialité.

1. **SUIVI ET CONTROLE**

- Assurer la gestion du budget des activités en étroite coordination avec le Chef de Projet ;
- Suivre l’actualisation du plan de suivi-évaluation du projet en collaboration avec l’Officier MEAL ;
- S’assurer que les ressources ont été utilisées convenablement et en conformité avec les SOP et directives techniques ;
- Faire le suivi des contrats et congés de l’équipe ;
- Rédiger les rapports mensuel, intermédiaire et rapport final ;
- Informer et consulter le Chef de Projet de toutes situations et circonstances pouvant affecter le bon fonctionnement de mise en œuvre.

1. **AUTRES TACHES**

En dehors de ses tâches et responsabilités mentionnées ci-haut, le **Team Leader** pourrait être appelé à :

- Participer aux formations et ateliers identifiés par le supérieur hiérarchique ;
- Créer la synergie avec les autres acteurs en vue de promouvoir le partage d’informations et proposer une réponse rapide et cohérente aux problèmes identifiés ;
- Contribuer à la poursuite de la redevabilité y compris les engagements au CHS ;
- Dénoncer au supérieur hiérarchique approprié, toute violation au Code de Conduite et à la politique de protection de l’enfance ; cette tâche est une obligation de tout un chacun ;
- Maintenir la confidentialité de toutes les informations acquises à l’occasion de l’exercice de ses fonctions et responsabilités, soit par des collègues ou concernant toute autre activité menée par DCA en général, qui n'ont pas encore été rendus public par la Direction

1. **QUALIFICATIONS, COMPETENCES REQUISES**

- Être de nationalité centrafricaine;
- Diplôme universitaire en Sciences sociales, Sciences humaines, Science politique, psychologie, droit ou autre domaine pertinent ;
- 5 ans d’expérience dans l’humanitaire et au sein d’une ONG internationale sur un poste similaire ;
- Au moins 2 ans d’expérience dans la gestion d’équipe ;
- Niveau élevé en Français et Sango (Oral, lecture et écrit). Anglais, parlé et/ou écrit apprécié ;
- Expérience dans la mise en œuvre de projets d’urgence (réponse rapide), y compris le volet cash ;
- Solide expérience dans la facilitation de formations auprès de diverses parties prenantes et personnel humanitaire ;
- Expérience dans le développement d’outils, SOPs et les directives techniques pour des activités protection ;
- Aptitude à travailler de longues heures sous pression, de manière flexible, adaptable et autonome ;
- Avoir une aptitude à travailler efficacement dans des circonstances extrêmes, y compris le stress, les risques élevés de sécurité et de conditions de vie difficile ;
- Grande capacité de communication, écrite et orale, et à entretenir des relations avec une expérience dans la gestion des équipes de travail ;
- Maitrise du pack office (Word, Excel, Power Point, navigation Internet…), Outlook.
- Excellentes compétences en communication orale et écrite ainsi que des capacités analytiques ;
- Haut niveau de motivation, prêt(e) à relever des défis et offrir des solutions ;
- Disponibilité à être basé à Bria.

1. **APTITUDES PERSONNELLES SOUHAITÉES**

- Bonne connaissance des outils de suivi et d’évaluation;
- Avoir une bonne compréhension des mécanismes de redevabilité ;
- Capacité à travailler dans un environnement multiculturel et professionnellement isolé.

**Le poste est réservé uniquement aux candidats de la nationalité centrafricaine.**

